 operating system software and some widely used applications are bundled with a computer system for sale.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="25017">bundle</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2486021">bwndelu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13592_25636_508254"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The surface of a button where text or an image (typically indicating the button's function) may be displayed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="25636">button face</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="508254">wyneb botwm</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13594_503136_2718923"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The presence status that indicates a user hasn't used his/her mouse, keyboard, computer, mobile phone, or communications device for a specified time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="503136">Inactive</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2718923">Segur</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="gramm