arious locations. The locations might be on your computer, an external hard drive, removable media, or someone else’s computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="746479">library</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1166910">llyfrgell</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20724_746483_1166911"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To mark an item so that it always appears in a specific place in the UI or in a list.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="746483">pin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1166911">pinio</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20725_746484_1166912"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To remove an item, such as a tile, library, movie, game, or app, from a given area of the UI, to make it inaccessible in that area.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="746484">unpin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1166912">dadbinio</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</ter