connect to Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) or Active Directory directory service.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1245017">ADMA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1958617">Asiant Rheoli Active Directory</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25957_1245017_1985361"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Identity Lifecycle Manager management agent provided by Microsoft to connect to Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) or Active Directory directory service.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1245017">ADMA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1985361">ADMA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25959_1247422_1958957"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A mailbox folder structure on some IMAP servers in which mail folders are accessed with the administrator username and password, and shell login access to the mail server is not allowed. Access to specific mailboxes is managed by access control lists. This means that users are assigned the permissions to only access their mailbox folder, while an administrator has access to all mailboxes. This allows organizations to use administrative credentials to migrate email from an IMAP server to Outlook Live.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1247422">virtual shared folder</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1958957">rhith ffolder a rennir</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2596_335540_2787764"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To provide your name and contact information to an organization so that you can receive product information, updates, and special offers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="335540">register</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2787764">cofrestru</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25978_1251313_1958735"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To place a windows Live ID in a forced rename state, while the Windows Live ID and all of its existing settings, including the password, Xbox Live points, or Zune points are preserved. The user can sign in using the Windows Live ID and its password, but they're immediately asked to rename the Windows Live ID. They must specify an email address that's outside the Outlook Live domain.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1251313">evict</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1958735">gorfodi ailenwi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25979_1253307_1519333"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The service in Microsoft Sharepoint Foundation that needs to be started to allow for a sandboxed solution to be deployed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1253307">Sandboxed Code Service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1519333">Gwasanaeth Cod Blwch Tywod</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25979_1253307_1930942"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The service in Microsoft Sharepoint Foundation that needs to be started to allow for a sandboxed solution to be deployed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1253307">Sandboxed Code Service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1930942">Microsoft SharePoint Foundation Sandboxed Code Service</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25979_1496238_1519333"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The service in Microsoft Sharepoint Foundation that needs to be started to allow for a sandboxed solution to be deployed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1496238">Microsoft SharePoint Foundation Sandboxed Code Service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1519333">Gwasanaeth Cod Blwch Tywod</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25979_1496238_1930942"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The service in Microsoft Sharepoint Foundation that needs to be started to allow for a sandboxed solution to be deployed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1496238">Microsoft SharePoint Foundation Sandboxed Code Service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1930942">Microsoft SharePoint Foundation Sandboxed Code Service</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25985_1253605_2338547"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A graphical representation of data where the intensity of color corresponds to the related analytical data. For example, low values in a range appear as blue (cold) and high values as red (hot).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1253605">heat map</term><termNote type="par