aticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29333_1507115_1931116"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The amount of information that is stored in a log file for a transaction. Log levels can be represented by numbers or by words from the most to the least verbose.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1507115">log level</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1931116">lefel log</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29334_1507116_1519340"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A complete set of conditions that are used to generate search results, including query text, sort order, and ranking parameters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1507116">search query</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1519340">ymholiad chwilio</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29335_1507117_1931117"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A record of information about user searches, such as search terms and time of access.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1507117">search query log</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1931117">log ymholiadau chwilio</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29336_1507118_1931118"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A report that is generated from query log information. For example, a search query log report might include the number of queries that were executed every day over the past thirty days.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1507118">search query log report</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1931118">adroddiad log ymholiadau chwilio</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29337_1507119_1931119"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The user search security filter that specifies group and user permissions for a specific FAST Search user. FAST Search Authorization (FSA) filters out inappropriate search results by intersecting the user’s query with the user's search security filter, and checking each document’s access control list to determine if the user has permission to view that document. The user search security filter is FSA's primary means of enforcing document-level security ("security trimming"), which helps to ensure that search results display only documents that the user has permissions to read.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1507119">user search security filter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1931119">hidlydd diogelwch chwiliad defnyddiwr</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29338_1507120_1931120"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The condition of a Web Part and the Web Part chrome surrounding it. Possible values are zero (0) for normal state or one (1) for minimized state.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1507120">Web Part chrome state</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1931120">cyflwr crôm Rhan Gwe</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29339_1507121_1931121"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A default group of users on a SharePoint site. By default, the Visitors group is assigned the Read permission level.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1507121">Visitors group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1931121">Grŵp ymwelwyr</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2934_141