 a quick response or by taking a suggested action, such as scheduling a meeting, creating a task, sending a file etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2834953">Suggested Actions</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2837182">Camau Gweithredu sy'n cael eu Hargymell</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="501_140730_1824086"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The range of cells that you select to hold the summarized data in a consolidation. The destination area can be on the same worksheet as the source data or on a different worksheet. A worksheet can contain only one consolidation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="140730">destination area</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1824086">ardal y man derbyn</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50100_2834955_2911359"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature within Microsoft Teams that helps a teacher make a Reading Assignment, lets the student record themselves reading, and then submit to the teacher for miscue analysis. Additionally, the computer will “listen” to the person read, and then gives computer generated “miscue analysis” feedback automatically to the teacher.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2834955">Reading Progress</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2911359">Datblygiad Darllen</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50102_2834957_2843717"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An application mounting capability for MSIX packaged apps whereby apps are mounted to a device/virtual machine (VM) from a remote file server location and all data transfer happens over the Azure's back end.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2834957">MSIX app attach</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2843717">atodi apiau</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50102_2834957_2843721"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An application mounting capability for MSIX packaged apps whereby apps are mounted to a device/virtual machine (VM) from a remote file server location and all data transfer happens over the Azure's back end.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2834957">MSIX app attach</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2843721">atodi apiau MSIX</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50102_2834958_2843717"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An application mounting capability for MSIX packaged apps whereby apps are mounted to a device/virtual machine (VM) from a remote file server location and all data transfer happens over the Azure's back end.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2834958">app attach</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2843717">atodi apiau</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50102_2834958_2843721"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An application mounting capability for MSIX packaged apps whereby apps are mounted to a device/virtual machine (VM) from a remote file server location and all data transfer happens over the Azure's back end.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2834958">app attach</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2843721">atodi apiau MSIX</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50105_2834963_2837181"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An Office 365 feature that detects when a reply-all or conversation mail storm is brewing in your mail service and temporarily blocks subsequent reply-alls to the thread while issuing a bounce back message (NDR) to the sender who is attempting to reply all. After a "cool down" period (e.g. 2 to 4 hours), the feature will remove the block and allow emails on the thread again (some exceptions can be made during the cool down).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2834963">Reply-All Storm Protection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2837181">Dioglewch rhag Storm Ateb Pawb</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50117_2835490_2840045"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A regular telephone number meant for a single user to receive and place calls. User numbers can be assigned to any PSTN Calling user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2835490">user number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2840045">rhif defnyddiwr</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50118_2835492_2840044"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Skype telephone number that is used for audio conferencing, auto attendants, or a call queue</descrip></desc