rawing or writing on a screen, rather with a keyboard.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="60255">handwriting</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1824505">llawysgrifen ddigidol</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6460_66237_1824023"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of settings that enable users to send, store, and receive email, and that define how to store and use addresses.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="66237">information service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1824023">gwasanaeth gwybodaeth</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6474_329880_509933"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technology allowing users to inject faults into an executable without requiring rebuilding the binary or modifying the source code; thus, providing a means of simulating errors and testing recovery.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="329880">fault injection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="509933">creu gwallau</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">