drivers that process the same IRPs, along with all intermediate drivers in the chain.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="170485">layered driver</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="509192">gyrrwr haenog</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7581_237287_1824228"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows creation of mathematical formulas in documents, including the insertion of mathematical symbols inside designated "math zones" which perform automatic formatting to convert fractions, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237287">Equation Builder</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1824228">Lluniwr Hafaliad</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7584_130154_508952"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A portion of unique computer code contained in a virus. Antivirus programs search for known virus signatures to identify infected programs and files.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="130154">virus signature</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="508952">rhith lofnod</term><termNote type="geo