 type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7712_130661_508955"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An area of storage on a hard disk. A volume is formatted by using a file system, such as NTFS, and has a drive letter assigned to it. A single hard disk can have multiple volumes. Some volumes can span multiple hard disks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="130661">volume</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="508955">cyfrol</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7719_175788_1166759"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A handle (often, a tall, thin rectangle) that appears on a rebar or command band. By touching and dragging a gripper bar with a stylus or mouse, a user can reposition or resize a rebar or command band.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="175788">gripper bar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1166759">cydiwr</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7719_770797_1166759"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A handle (often, a tall, thin rectangle) that appears on a rebar or command band. By touching and dragging a gripper bar with a stylus or mouse, a user can reposition or resize a rebar or command band.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="770797">gripper</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1166759">cydiwr</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7726_373353_1095086"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The act of following a link from one Web site to a site or page on another server when crawling for content.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="373353">site hop</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1095086">neidio rhwng safleoedd</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7735_1136138_509790"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of UI controls that appear in context when an object is selected and contain actions that act upon the object.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1136138">mini-toolbar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="cy-GB"><ntig><termGrp><term id="509790">Bar offer bach</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GBR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote